WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.950
STEPHANIE WONG: If you're
new to Google Cloud,

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:05.100
there is a lot to
absorb especially

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.950
if you're excited to get
started in any of the many tools

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:11.550
out there, like big data
Analytics, Kubernetes,

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:14.430
Serverless, or machine learning.

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:17.040
I'm here to break it all
down so you can start

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.198
building things up right away.

00:00:19.198 --> 00:00:23.978
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:25.495 --> 00:00:27.120
So first things first,
cloud.google.com

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:30.700
is your starting point.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:32.369
This is where you
will find information

00:00:32.369 --> 00:00:34.235
about our products and offers.

00:00:34.235 --> 00:00:35.610
If you want to
jump right in, you

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:38.970
can go directly to the console
or search our documentation

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:42.840
for quickstarts, solutions,
reference architectures,

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.360
and browse code samples.

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:49.770
You'll also find our latest
offers listed like free trials.

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:52.020
Pricing is also detailed
there, including

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:54.420
Google's pricing
list, a detailed cost

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:57.690
calculator for every Google
Cloud product and service,

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:02.760
and information on the free tier
for every applicable product.

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:06.420
Cloud.google.com is also
the place to access support,

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:09.360
to read customer stories,
to find partners,

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.430
and to understand
how Google Cloud is

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:14.460
different from
other public clouds.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:17.160
You'll also find helpful
getting started resources,

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:21.030
like quickstarts, trainings,
and certifications.

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:23.730
But, in my opinion, the
best way to really get

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:26.490
started is the
Google Cloud console.

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:29.760
This is where you'll probably
spend the most time exploring

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.470
and using the platform.

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:33.450
It's where you configure
billing accounts,

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:37.140
create and manage projects, and
manage all of your Google Cloud

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:41.670
resources, regardless of
their data center location.

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:44.910
Every product and every
service has its own section

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:48.510
in the console left-hand
menu with dashboards,

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:52.020
detailed configuration,
and settings.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:55.260
You'll also find interactive
quickstart experiences

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:58.720
right from inside the console.

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:02.710
Take this example quickstart
for Compute Engine.

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:05.500
Right from here, it'll
show you exactly where

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:08.139
to go in the console
for each step.

00:02:08.139 --> 00:02:11.680
And within minutes, you'll
be running a two-tier web

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.680
application running a
Python web server running

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:17.380
on Compute Engine.

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:20.680
The Cloud Console also
offers a marketplace

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:24.430
with ready-to-go software stacks
to accelerate development,

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:26.590
so you spend less
time installing

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:28.510
and more time developing.

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:32.020
This allows you to deploy
production-grade solutions

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:36.160
in a few clicks with a single
bill for all of your Google

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:37.990
Cloud and third-party costs.

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:41.680
And it also offers direct
access to partner support.

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:43.360
To make sure you set
up your employees

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:45.700
with the right permissions
to use different Google Cloud

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:49.390
Resources, Cloud Console
integrates Identity and Access

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:54.310
Management, or Cloud IAM,
and provides a unified view

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:59.030
into security policies across
your entire organization.

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:01.120
This is also where you
would manage quotas

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:03.160
across the platform.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:06.580
Every product comes with
one or more usage limits

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:09.190
across the platform, so
you can prevent one team

00:03:09.190 --> 00:03:14.020
from spending the entire
org's budget on a rogue query

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:16.750
or compute job.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:20.200
You can also use our iOS
and Android mobile apps

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:23.440
to monitor and manage your
Google Cloud applications

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:25.270
on the go.

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:28.000
Lastly, you can contact
support or sign up

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:31.030
for support packages for both
development and production

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:34.660
phases right from the console.

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:38.440
Role-Based Support enables
configuration on a per user

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:39.340
basis.

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:41.410
And case management
is integrated

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:44.440
into the Cloud Console.

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:47.290
Premium support offers
additional support

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:51.310
and faster response times for
mission critical workloads.

00:03:51.310 --> 00:03:54.400
If you'd like to know more
about the Google Cloud Console,

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.740
check out the links below.

00:03:56.740 --> 00:04:00.140
While the console is
powerful and flexible,

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:03.580
you can do everything
from the command line.

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:07.990
For every action in the console,
there is a G Cloud equivalent.

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:11.470
G Cloud is your scriptable
and all mighty CLI,

00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:14.170
and it comes with
the Google Cloud SDK.

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:16.420
You can do things
like create resources,

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:20.320
change configurations,
and grant authorization.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:22.270
There are other
command line tools

00:04:22.270 --> 00:04:25.900
for products like
BigQuery and GKE.

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:29.320
The G Cloud SDK and these
CLIs come preinstalled

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:31.720
in Cloud Shell.

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:33.910
Cloud Shell is a
shell environment

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:37.120
hosted on Google Cloud
for managing your projects

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:38.590
and resources.

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:41.560
It's accessible from
a simple web browser

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:44.140
and is powered by a
small virtual machine

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:47.590
with persistent disk space and
up-to-date software for all

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:49.270
of your development needs.

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:52.660
It even comes with a really
handy web code editor.

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:58.000
If you'd like to know more
about developer tools,

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:01.420
check out the links in
the description below.

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:04.450
Now before you can use
the Google Cloud Console,

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:08.300
you will need a Google account.

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:10.270
You can create a
new Google account

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:13.960
or use an existing one,
such as your Gmail account.

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:17.320
We recommend that you enable
billing for your project

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:21.470
and that you sign up
for our free trial.

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:25.000
But if you don't sign up for
the free trial or are unable to,

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:28.960
you can still benefit from
the generous always free tier.

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:31.570
Once logged into the
Google Cloud Console,

00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:34.360
I recommend that you
check out the main menu

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:38.290
and in particular the
Getting Started section.

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:41.380
Check out the checklist
to complete common tasks

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:45.580
like creating a project,
finding products and APIs,

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:49.930
and adding your very
first resources.

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:51.580
Back on the Getting
Started page,

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:54.700
scroll down to the
section Put Google Cloud

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:59.440
to Work, and click on Browse
Interactive Tutorials.

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:01.600
This opens up a
panel with a list

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:03.850
of tutorials of your
product of choice

00:06:03.850 --> 00:06:06.730
without leaving the console.

00:06:06.730 --> 00:06:09.790
Finally, check out the
main categories of products

00:06:09.790 --> 00:06:12.250
Google Cloud has to offer--

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:21.760
Compute, Storage, Networking,
Operations, Tools, Big Data,

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:25.620
and Artificial Intelligence.

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:28.890
As you progress through your
discovery of Google Cloud,

00:06:28.890 --> 00:06:31.800
keep in mind these
key resources.

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:36.510
Documentation can be found
at cloud.google.com/docs,

00:06:36.510 --> 00:06:41.520
in-depth architectural diagrams
and tutorials at /architecture,

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:50.430
code samples at /docs/samples,
support at /support,

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:54.390
training at /training,
and free code labs

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:58.140
at g.co/codelabs/cloud.

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:01.540
Google Cloud can be a little
overwhelming at first,

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:04.290
but with this guidance
I hope that you are now

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:07.973
confident that your best ideas
can come to life in the Cloud.

00:07:07.973 --> 00:07:09.390
I'm excited to see
what you build,

00:07:09.390 --> 00:07:11.790
and I look forward
to your feedback.

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:15.360
If you like this video, please
like, subscribe, comment,

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:16.380
and share.

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:17.600
This is Stephanie Wong.

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:19.910
I'll see you all next time.

